## 3. Upstream Open-Source Software & Third-Party Libraries

Uli Engine is a modified derivative work built upon the following open-source
projects (notice of modification provided pursuant to Apache License 2.0 §4(b)):

- **Friday Night Funkin' (Engine Codebase)** — Licensed under the Apache License 2.0
  (The Funkin' Crew Inc.)
- **Psych Engine 1.0.4** — Licensed under the Apache License 2.0
  (Shadow Mario & Psych Engine Contributors)
- **HaxeFlixel, OpenFL, Lime, LuaJIT, Discord RPC** — MIT License
- **libogg & libvorbis** — BSD-3-Clause License
- **libVLC / hxvlc (Windows builds only)** — GNU Lesser General Public License
  v2.1 (LGPL-2.1). Unmodified dynamic libraries are distributed alongside Windows
  builds; Android builds do not include libVLC.
- **7-Zip-JBinding (Android builds only)** — GNU Lesser General Public License
  v2.1 (LGPL-2.1) and respective archive decoder terms.

All upstream copyright and attribution notices are retained in accordance with
their respective licenses.

